X:1
T:Deeper Underground
C:Jamiroquai
M:4/4
O:England, 1998
N:Second verse and chorus. Melody from the lead channel (channel 4) of a MIDI arrangement (hamienet.com, track 4494), moved down a major seventh from C-sharp minor to D minor so the lowest note lands on C4. Single source: the other arrangement found (track 353075582280359) has no lead line. The verse runs over the bass riff on the tonic, so every verse bar is Dm. The chorus is a three-bar unit sung three times; in its second and third bars the arrangement plays only a bass line (C, A, F-sharp, then E, A, A-flat in this key) with no chord on top, so no chord is marked there. Humanized onsets snapped to the sixteenth grid; releases up to an eighth short of the next note are filled in.
Q:1/4=105
